Z||000000||la9||03-26-2000||11:31 PM||||Well I try not to speak too soon that is why I waited to post this message after 650 miles on my newly rebuilt engine and transmission. Everything seems to be holding together well. It is probably the best running car I've ever had. I think I have most of the kinks worked out, even the now famous code 32. The only things that don't work is the air-conditioner and the cruise. I forgot the windshield leaks when it rains and you go downhill. Not bad for a 14 year old car. I just rebuild the 2.8 because it was my first rebuild and I didn't want to deal with more problems than you'd normally have. I did everything you could think of when I rebuilt it including getting it line-honed and balanced. The engines seems to pull pretty good, it would be the cats meow if it was only a 5 speed. Thanks to everyone in the forum who helped with questions along the way. I do have one more though. Does anyone have any idea where I placed my Pontiac service manual at ? It's probably next to the car keys right ?||||reg||10
